resolved_issues.body:
Thanks for this great library ! I had an issue trying to fix all corner cases of https://gitlab.com/scilab/scilab/-/issues/15639. It seems that `zscal` does not handle INFINITY correctly (even after #4413). 

You can reproduce it with :
```c#include <stdio.h>
#include <math.h>

extern void zscal_(int*, double*, double*, int*);

int main(int argc, char ** argv)
{
    int ONE = 1;

    double i_tab[] = {0, 1};
    double* i = i_tab;
    double inf_tab[] = {INFINITY, 0};
    double* inf = inf_tab;

    zscal_(&ONE, i, inf, &ONE);
    printf("result of i*Inf  = %g+%g*i\n", inf[0], inf[1]);    
    inf[0] = INFINITY;
    inf[1] = 0;

    zscal_(&ONE, inf, i, &ONE);
    printf("result of Inf*i  = %g+%g*i\n", i[0], i[1]);
    i[0] = 0;
    i[1] = 1;

    // crafted complex i * Inf
    inf[0] = 0;
    inf[1] = INFINITY;

    zscal_(&ONE, i, inf, &ONE);
    printf("result of i*iInf = %g+%g*i\n", inf[0], inf[1]);
    inf[0] = 0;
    inf[1] = INFINITY;

    zscal_(&ONE, inf, i, &ONE);
    printf("result of iInf*i = %g+%g*i\n", i[0], i[1]);
    i[0] = 0;
    i[1] = 1;

    return 0;
}
```
The results are:
```screen
    result of i*Inf  = nan+inf*i    // may better be -nan+inf*i although it does not really matter
    result of Inf*i  = -nan+inf*i
=>  result of i*iInf = -inf+0*i   	// should be -inf+-nan*i
    result of iInf*i = -inf+-nan*i
```

