```
#include <stdio.h>
#include <cblas.h>
#include <math.h>
int main(int argc, char ** argv)
{
    double i[] = {0, 1};
    double nan[] = {NAN, 0};
    cblas_zscal(1, i, &nan, 1);
    printf("result of i*NAN=%g+%g*i\n", nan[0], nan[1]);
    
    nan[0] = NAN;
    nan[1] = 0;
    cblas_zscal(1, &nan, &i, 1);
    printf("result of NAN*i=%g+%g*i\n", i[0], i[1]);
    return 0;
}
```
returns:
result of i*NAN=-0+nan*i
result of NAN*i=nan+nan*i

While I get nan+nan*i & nan+nan*i with refblas, mkl or atlas.

cblas.h is provided by blas

See also #86

